Kausalyā sips pure water and begins auspicious blessings --- Kausalyā invokes Sādhyas Viśvas Maruts Dhātr̥ Vidhātr̥ Pūṣan Bhaga Aryaman --- Kausalyā invokes seasons fortnights months years nights days and hours --- Kausalyā invokes Smr̥ti Dhr̥ti Dharma Skanda Sōma Br̥haspati --- Kausalyā invokes Saptar̥ṣis Nārada stars planets to guard forest Rāma --- Kausalyā prays monkeys scorpions gnats flies snakes insects spare him --- Kausalyā prays elephants lions tigers bears buffaloes flesh-eaters spare him --- Kausalyā prays journeys safe, prowess succeed, sky earth Brahmā guard him --- Kausalyā worships gods with garlands scents praises, cites Vr̥tra Suparṇa fortune --- Kausalyā ties herbal guard with mantras, embraces and sends Rāma to Sītā
